  "title": "Kwame Nkrumah",
  "summary": "Kwame Nkrumah, born in 1909 in Nkroful in the Gold Coast, led the movement for independence from Britain. He was prime minister of the Gold Coast from 1952 and of independent Ghana from 1957, then president from 1960. A military coup overthrew him in 1966, and he died in exile in Bucharest on 27 April 1972.",
